            3CZRCHU,2UK EDG,2ITYPAD,2ITYFRA,2ITYCAT,2SWDUPP)
           (2ITYITY) Consiglio Nazionale delle Ricerche, Bari
REFERENCE  (J,PL/B,872,140070,2026)
           #doi:10.1016/j.physletb.2025.140070
           (J,EPJ/CS,294,01003,2024)
           #doi:10.1051/epjconf/202429401003
            Preliminary fission yields on figs
           (T,SANCHEZ-CABALLERO,2026)
           PhD's thesis submitted to Universidad Complutense de
            Madrid
EXP-YEAR   (2022) September to November 2022
REL-REF    (I,,C.Guerrero+,J,EPJ/A,49,27,2013)
            Description of facility
           (I,,J.Perkowski+,J,NIM/A,1067,169649,2024)
            Description of fission ionization chamber
FACILITY   (SYNCH,2ZZZCER) CERN nTOF facility.
           proton beam with pulse width of 7 nsec
INC-SOURCE (SPALL) neutrons were produced in a gas-cooled Pb
            target and moderated by a 4 cm layer of borated water
SAMPLE     8.541(14) mg of 239Pu (99.90259%) distributed into ten
            samples of PuO2, 20 mm diameter, electrodeposited
            (molecular plating) on Al backing (10 um), yielding a
            surface density of ~300 ug/cm2 for nine of the
            samples and 40 ug/cm2 for one of them with less mass.
           (94-PU-239,ENR=0.9990259) 99.90259(14)%
           (94-PU-240,ENR=0.0005818)   0.05818(4)%
           (94-PU-241,ENR=0.0002501)   0.02501(5)%
           (94-PU-242,ENR=0.0001288)   0.01288(7)%
DETECTOR   (FISCH) Multi-section fission ionization chamber.
            Ar+(10%)CF4 gas with the ten PuO2 samples inside the
            cylindrical sealed chamber with 94 mm diameter and
            110 mm in length.
METHOD     (TOF) Flight path of 185 m
MONITOR    Energy dependence of the neutron flux was derived from
            dedicated measurements using different detectors
            based on the standard reactions 6Li(n,t)4He,
            10B(n,a)7Li and 235U(n,f), and there is no unique
            cross section ratio for compilation.
           (94-PU-239(N,F),,INT)
           Normalized to the 239Pu(n,f) cross section integral
            from 9.0 to 20.0 eV of 1059(6) b*eV
MONIT-REF  (,I.Duran+,J,NDS,193,95,2024)
CORRECTION Cross section without self-shielding correction. This
            and other corrections like Doppler Broadening and the
            resolution function are needed to reproduce the
            integral values reported in the reference paper.
COMMENT    *Adrian Sanchez-Caballero (2025-12-18):
